###############################################################################
# Initial atomic coordinates
###############################################################################

data_tcod_atom_site_initial_fract_
loop_ _name
'_tcod_atom_site_initial_fract_x' 
'_tcod_atom_site_initial_fract_y' 
'_tcod_atom_site_initial_fract_z'
_type numb
_type_conditions           esd
loop_
_related_item
_related_function
          '_tcod_atom_site_initial_Cartn_'
          alternate
_list                      yes
_list_reference            '_atom_site_label'
_definition
; Initial atom-site coordinates use to set up teh computaion as
  fractions of the _cell_length_* values.
;

data_tcod_atom_site_initial_Cartn_
loop_ _name
'_tcod_atom_site_initial_Cartn_x'
'_tcod_atom_site_initial_Cartn_y'
'_tcod_atom_site_initial_Cartn_z'
_type numb
_units                     A
_units_detail              'Angstroems'
_type_conditions           esd
loop_
_related_item
_related_function
          '_tcod_atom_site_initial_fract_'
          alternate
_list                      yes
_list_reference            '_atom_site_label'
_definition
; Initial Cartesian atom-site coordinates use to set up the computaion.

A set of orthogonal Cartesian axes related to the cell axes is
specified by the _atom_sites_Cartn_transform_axes and
_atom_sites_Cartn_tran_matrix_ descriptions.
;

###############################################################################
# Force field descriptions:
###############################################################################

data_tcod_ff_id
    _name '_tcod_ff_id'
    _type char
    _list                        yes
    _list_mandatory              yes
    _definition
; A unique identifier (primary key) of a force field in a loop, in
case the COD datablock containing ir refers to more than one force
field.
;     

data_tcod_ff_type
    _name '_tcod_ff_type'
    _type char
    loop_ _enumeration
          _enumeration_detail
          Fixed-charge           'describe the corresponding model here'
          Polarizable            'describe the corresponding model here'
          Distributed-multipole  'describe the corresponding model here'
          Hybrid                 'describe the corresponding model here'
          Reactive               'describe the corresponding model here'
          other                  'model not one of the mentioned above'
    _definition
; Fixed charge (standard biomolecular and materials: amber, opls, gromos etc.)
  Polarizable (AMOEBA, iAMOEBA etc.)
  Distributed multipole based FFs (multipoles instead of fixed point charges
  S. Price et al.)
  Hybrid (Different types for interatomic and intraatomic interactions)  
  Reactive (ReaxFF etc.)
  L.V. The list is non-exhaustive
;

data_tcod_ff_name
    _name '_tcod_ff_name'
    _type char
    _definition
; Standard name for the FF used. If there is no standard name use 'custom'
  Examples: charmm, opls, amber, gromos etc.
  L.V. One must add a reference to the original paper here
;

data_tcod_ff_version
    _name '_tcod_ff_version'
    _type char
    _definition
; Version of a force field. Usually year of the publication.  
;     

data_tcod_ff_citation_id
    _name '_tcod_ff_citation_id'
    _type char
    _list_link_parent '_citation_id'
    _definition
; A reference to the citation describing the force field in the
_citation_... category loop
;     

###############################################################################
# Citation management:
###############################################################################

data_tcod_citation_linkage
    _name      '_tcod_citation_linkage'
    _category  citation
    loop_ _enumeration
          _enumeration_detail
    force-field      'citation of the paper describing the force field'
    software-code    'citation of the paper describing the program code'
    model            'citation describing the overal method used'
    pseudopotential  'citation describing pseudopotential'
    XC-functional    'citation describing exchange correlation f-nal'
    basis-set        'citation describing the basis set'

_definition
;
    loop_
    _citation_id
    _tcod_citation_linkage
    _citation_coordinate_linkage
    _citation_journal_abbrev
    _citation_journal_volume
    _citation_journal_issue
    _citation_year
    _citation_page_first
    _citation_page_last
    1 force-field    'J. Some Name'    10 12 2014 1 12
    2 software-code  'J. Another Name' 10 12 2014 1 12

  L.V. Correct citation to the publication of the original FF is of extreme
  importance. 

  S.G. I suggest using 'citation' category data items from the core
  CIF dictionary, and adding just a few TCOD relevant data items such
  as _tcod_citation_linkage that would show which part of the
  computation (force field, software code, etc.) does the paper
  describe. Other items should point, whenever possible, to
  machine-readable URLs with the force field or program code
  definitions (for software, this might be liks to a source code for
  open source packages, liks to a compiled binary packages for
  specific platform, the ones used in the computations, and yet
  another link would point to a web site describing the software (this
  is relevan for both open-source and proprietary programs).

;

